# Git workflow

`main` is protected. All changes land through a pull request from a feature branch.

- Never commit, push, merge, or amend on `main`.
- Before making changes, create and check out a feature branch from up-to-date `origin/main` (`feat/…`, `fix/…`, `chore/…`).
- If the working tree is already on `main` with local changes, move that work onto a feature branch before committing.
- Push the feature branch and open a PR targeting `main`. Do not push to `main`.
- One concern per branch/PR. Do not mix unrelated work.
